season4_supplies_UI_13:
Rules: 

1. After the season starts, hidden <b>Large Lucky Cat</b> and <b>Mini Lucky Cat</b> will appear on the map. The location of the Lucky Cat varies in each warzone, waiting for commanders to explore; 
2. Commanders can use <b>Flares</b> or <b>Base Lights</b> to illuminate the night, with a chance to discover Large Lucky Cat; 
3. <b>Illuminating the Path to Battle</b> in the night has a chance to trigger Mini Lucky Cat<color=#C44E3B> (A maximum of 1 Mini Lucky Cat can be discovered per day)</color>; 
4. After the warzone achieves the stage target of defeating a certain number of <b>Oni Generals</b>, <b>additional Large Lucky Cat</b> will appear; 
5. After discovering a Lucky Cat, you need to dispatch electricians to charge it. <b>Only after it is fully charged can the rewards be claimed</b>; 
6. <b>All commanders can interact with Large Lucky Cat</b>, while Mini Lucky Cat can only be interacted with by the commander who discovered them; 
<color=#C44E3B><b>7. Daily reward claims are restored 5 times, up to a maximum of 15 times (Only applies to Large Lucky Cat; Mini Lucky Cat are not affected)</b></color>; 
<color=#7A4E2C><b>8. Rewards will be displayed in the Loot interface, and unclaimed Lucky Cat can be claimed by Recon Planes</b></color>.

season_s4_golden_tree_UI_53:
Rules: 

1. Sakura Isle is shrouded in eternal night, causing the ancient Divine Tree to fall into slumber. Commanders must <b><color=#D06DE2>charge and activate</color></b> it to restore the light;
2. The event consists of two phases: <b><color=#D06DE2>Charging</color></b> to activate the Divine Tree and <b><color=#D06DE2>Fortune Slip Drawing</color></b> to get rewards, starting by default from the charging phase;
3. In the first phase, commanders can dispatch electricians to <b><color=#D06DE2>charge</color></b> the Divine Tree, gradually lighting it up;
4. When the <b><color=#D06DE2>charging progress</color></b> of a warzone reaches the target, the Divine Tree fully awakens, granting generous rewards to participating commanders and automatically entering the <b><color=#D06DE2>Fortune Slip Drawing</color></b> phase;
5. After awakening, from Tuesday to Saturday each week, commanders receive one <b><color=#D06DE2>Fortune Drawing Chance</color></b> daily to obtain exclusive blessings from the Divine Tree;
6. Each fortune drawing randomly yields one of five slips—Fire, Water, Wood, Metal, or Earth. Upon drawing five slips in total, commanders earn combination rewards that bring good luck and victory in the Battle of Sakura Isle.

season_s4_update_notice_2:
Dear Commander,

To enhance your season experience, we have made the following optimizations:

1. Removed the "Disable Ally Electrician Assistance" toggle and added a new option: "Automatically Turn Off Lights When Blood Night Starts";
2. Daily rewards for Lucky Cat now limit only the large ones; Mini ones are no longer restricted;
3. Fixed an issue where monsters would not actively attack commanders’ bases in the dark during Blood Night;
4. Improved prompts related to the power system;
5. Enhanced visual effects of monster and lighting interactions;
6. Added a quick access to [Tactics Cards] on the season homepage;
7. Increased the maximum power storage of the Lighthouse according to its level.

Thank you very much for your valuable feedback!

